        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.086,
            0.883,
            0.139
          ],
          "content": "**Q.3. Starting from different floors, find the movements required to reach Floor – 5. For example, if I start at Floor + 2, I must press – 7 to reach Floor – 5. The expression is (+ 2) + (– 7) = – 5.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.148,
            0.883,
            0.183
          ],
          "content": "**Find more such starting positions and the movements needed to reach Floor – 5 and write the expressions.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.193,
            0.525,
            0.321
          ],
          "content": "Ans. Starting floor + Movement = Target Floor +1 + (-6) = (-5) -2 + (-3) = (-5) 0 + (-5) = (-5) (Try more possibilities)"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.357,
            0.236,
            0.374
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Page No. 246"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.383,
            0.234,
            0.401
          ],
          "content": "**Figure it out**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.41,
            0.883,
            0.528
          ],
          "content": "**Q. Evaluate these expressions by thinking of them as the resulting movement of combining button presses:** a. (+ 1) + (+ 4) = b. (+ 4) + (+ 1) = c. (+ 4) + (– 3) + (– 2) = d. (– 1) + (+ 2) + (– 3) = Ans. a. (+5) b. (+5) c. (-1) d. (-2)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.564,
            0.464,
            0.581
          ],
          "content": "**Q. Write the inverses of these numbers:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.617,
            0.347,
            0.773
          ],
          "content": "Ans. Inverse of +4 = -4 Inverse of -4 = +4 Inverse of -3 = +3 Inverse of 0 = 0 Inverse of +2 = (-2) Inverse of -1 = +1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.809,
            0.479,
            0.827
          ],
          "content": "**Q. Connect the inverses by drawing lines.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.837,
            0.219,
            0.854
          ],
          "content": "**(+5)**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.89,
            0.217,
            0.908
          ],
          "content": "**(–9)**"
        },
